<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Coronation of Charlemagne</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">800 CE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The coronation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> took place in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> on Christmas Day 800 CE, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-leo-iii">Pope Leo III</a> crowned the Frankish king as emperor. It revived the imperial title in the West for the first time since the fifth century. The event marked the high point of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a> and later served as the model for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/coronation-of-charlemagne.jpg" alt="Coronation of Charlemagne" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charlemagne. Autorité émettrice de monnaie indéterminé. Atelier monétaire. Émetteur · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charlemagne_denier_Mayence_812_814.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
